name issue_23_low_bandwidth
describe 150 kbps link: audio must stay clean, video degrades gracefully: the receiver asks for keyframes as libwebrtc does
# Issue #23 (partial): the receiver asks for a keyframe only where libwebrtc does (NackRequester + RtpVideoStreamReceiver2).
# Target (issue #23): video.keyframe_requests within 2x of libwebrtc or within 2 requests (libwebrtc: 0.3) on seeds 1-5
# without raising video.longest_freeze_ms; this scenario locks the request count only (see docs/fixes/23-libwebrtc-keyframe-policy.md, Remaining).
keyframe v2
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=150kbps delay=40ms queue=500ms
expect video.keyframe_requests <= 2
# Longest freeze is locked at the level reached (libwebrtc: 12936 total / 3279 longest).
# Flip (#61, needs-human): was `video.freeze_total_ms < 6500`; seeds 1-5 with every v2 switch on: 8404-21563 ms; libwebrtc 12936 ms (10 seeds).
# Owner-approved (PR #116): libwebrtc itself freezes 12.9 s here (10 seeds), so the line sits above libwebrtc's value, not at the old 6500.
# Target (issue #23): freeze total within the parity band of libwebrtc's 12.9 s, longest freeze not above libwebrtc's 3279 ms.
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 22000
expect video.longest_freeze_ms < 4500
